## 1. What this is

A marketing website for **RECSEEKERS**, a specialist "Rec2Rec" (recruitment-to-recruitment) agency in the **education sector**. It places recruitment consultants into education recruitment agencies across the **UK and Australia**. Two audiences: *candidates* (education recruiters looking to move) and *employers* (agencies hiring recruiters).

There is no login, no database, no job board. It is a brochure site with two lead-capture forms that push into HubSpot and email via Resend.

### The stack

| Layer | Choice |
|---|---|
| Framework | **Next.js `^16.1.6`** (lockfile resolves 16.2.1), App Router, `output: "standalone"`, Turbopack for both `dev` and `build` |
| UI | **React 19.2.3**, **Tailwind CSS v4** (CSS-first `@theme inline` — *no `tailwind.config.js`*) |
| Animation | **framer-motion 12**, plus hand-written CSS keyframes in `globals.css` |
| Language | TypeScript 5, `strict: true` |
| CMS | **Sanity Studio v5** in `cms/` — **wired up but currently rendering nothing** (see §5.3) |
| Email | **Resend** (`resend` 6.x) |
| CRM | **HubSpot** CRM v3 REST API (via `fetch`, no SDK) |
| Anti-spam | **Google reCAPTCHA** — *client-side only, never verified server-side* |
| Social proof | **Elfsight** LinkedIn feed widget (third-party CDN script) |
| Node | `>=22.13.0` (pinned in `.nvmrc` as `22.13.0`), npm `>=10` |

### Repo shape

```
RECSEEKERS-Website/
├── .github/workflows/     CI: GHCR docker build + PR build check
├── cms/                   Sanity Studio (separate npm project)
├── frontend/              Next.js app (separate npm project)
└── README.md
```

Two independent npm projects. There is **no workspace/monorepo tooling** — you `npm install` in each folder separately.

