### Environment variables — the real list

`frontend/.env.example` is **out of date**: it documents three variables, one of which is never read, and omits four that the app actually uses. This is the accurate list:

| Variable | Used by | Required? | What happens if missing |
|---|---|---|---|
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID` | `frontend/sanity/client.ts` | Yes (module-level `!` assertion) | Currently harmless — nothing fetches — but the module is still imported by `app/page.tsx` |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET` | `frontend/sanity/client.ts` | Yes | as above |
| `RESEND_API_KEY` | `app/api/contact/route.ts` | Yes, for the contact form | `500 {"error":"Email service is not configured."}` |
| `SAM_EMAIL` | `app/api/contact/route.ts` | Yes, for the contact form | same 500 — this is the internal notification recipient |
| `HUBSPOT_ACCESS_TOKEN` | `app/api/contact/route.ts` | Optional | `console.warn`, CRM step silently skipped |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY` | `app/contact/page.tsx`, `app/sign-up/page.tsx` | Yes, for the forms | reCAPTCHA renders with `sitekey=""`; on `/sign-up` the submit button stays disabled, on `/contact` the button is live but `handleInitialSubmit` blocks submission with an `alert()` |
| ~~`SANITY_API_TOKEN`~~ | — | **No** | Listed in `.env.example` but **read by nothing**. Ignore it. |

Known Sanity values (they are not secret — the project ID is public by design):

```
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID=3o1ax6lm
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET=production
```

**There is no `RECAPTCHA_SECRET_KEY` anywhere in the repo**, because the server never verifies the captcha. See §8.

