## 3. Architecture at a glance

```
Browser
  │
  ├─ Marketing pages (all copy hardcoded in JSX; /contact and /sign-up are Client Components)
  │     / /about /candidates /employers /edtech /subscription /contact /sign-up /privacy /terms
  │
  ├─ /privacy and /terms  ──reads──►  frontend/content/legal.en.json  (committed JSON, NOT Sanity)
  │
  ├─ /about LinkedIn feed ──script──►  Elfsight CDN widget  (elfsightcdn.com)
  │
  └─ Forms on /contact, /sign-up, and the BookCall modal
        │  POST { name, email, ... }
        ▼
     app/api/contact/route.ts  (the ONLY backend in the project)
        ├─► HubSpot CRM  (GET contact by email → POST create if absent)
        └─► Resend       (email #1 → SAM_EMAIL, email #2 → the user)

  Sanity Studio (cms/)  ──►  Sanity dataset  ──X──  NOTHING ON THE SITE READS IT
```

**The single most important thing to understand:** almost every word on this site is hardcoded in `.tsx` files. Editing marketing copy means editing React components and redeploying. The Sanity CMS exists, is configured, and has three schemas — but **zero rendered content comes from it**. See §5.3 and §7.

### Layout composition

`app/layout.tsx` wraps every route in:

```
<HeroStageProvider>          ← context/HeroStageContext.tsx
  <NavMobile />              ← md:hidden  full-screen hamburger menu
  <Nav />                    ← hidden md:block  desktop pill nav + hover preview
  {children}
  <Footer />
</HeroStageProvider>
```

Fonts: **Poppins** (body, Google Fonts, `--font-poppins`) and **Cooper Black** (headings, self-hosted `.ttf`, `--font-cooper`, exported from `lib/fonts.ts` as `cooper`). Headings almost always apply it via `className={cooper.className}` rather than a Tailwind utility; a handful of places use the `font-cooper` / `font-heading` utilities instead (`footer.tsx`, `NavMobile.tsx`, `carousel.tsx`).

