### 🟠 Lint will fail

`npm run lint` was not executed for this document (no `node_modules` in a fresh clone), but the following unused imports/vars were confirmed by inspection: `app/page.tsx` (`client`, `TEMPLATE_STATUS_QUERY`), `app/candidates/page.tsx` (`HeroSection`, `placeHolderProfile`), `app/about/page.tsx` (`ClientsSection`), `app/edtech/page.tsx` (`Link`, `Button`), `app/subscription/page.tsx` (`Link`, `Button`), `TeamSection.tsx` (`DoodleFloat`), `WhereWeWorkSection.tsx` (`DoodleFloat`), `BlobPortrait.tsx` (`num`). Plus `@next/next/no-img-element` (raw `<img>` in `Nav`, `NavMobile`, `footer`, `NavPreview`, `employers/page`) and `react/no-unescaped-entities` in several files. **CI never runs lint**, which is why this accumulated — adding `npm run lint` to `frontend-build-pr.yml` would stop it getting worse.

### 🟡 Architecture & maintainability

| Issue | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Three forked `TestimonialsSection`s** | Same component copy-pasted three times. Consolidate into one taking `testimonials` + `heading` props. Biggest single win. |
| **Two forked `BottomCTA`s** + `variantConfig` duplicated three times | Same story. |
| **Mobile/desktop copy forking** | `block md:hidden` + `hidden md:block` twins on `/about`, `/candidates`, `/contact`, `/employers`, `/sign-up`. On `/employers` the `<h1>` twins are identical (so the `<h1>` is duplicated for nothing), but the paragraph twins **diverge** — as they do everywhere else — creating two sources of truth for the same claim. On `/sign-up` the mobile variant is simply missing. Use responsive CSS, not duplicated markup. |
| **`<BottomCTA />` rendered twice on `/employers`** | Mounts two `BookCallModal`s and two motion observers to change one margin class. |
| **`HeroStageContext` never resets on navigation** | Provider lives in the root layout; only `HeroSection` writes to it, and only on `/`. Navigating away leaves stale state. |
| **Colour drift** | Brand hexes are hardcoded throughout instead of using the tokens; several colours in use aren't tokens at all. A rebrand is currently a find-and-replace across dozens of files. |
| **Font fragmentation** | `lib/fonts.ts` registers the same TTF twice; `/contact` and `/sign-up` each declare their own `localFont` instance instead of importing it; the two 404 pages reference a `fontFamily: 'cooper'` that resolves to nothing. |
| **Scroll-hijacking hero** | Manual wheel/touch listeners plus a full `html`/`body` scroll lock. Inherently fragile — regression-test it on real iOS Safari after any dependency upgrade. |
| **No `metadata` per page** | Every route serves `title: "RECSEEKERS"`. No OG tags, no `sitemap.ts`, no `robots.ts`. Low-effort, high-value SEO fix. |
| **Both project READMEs are unadapted boilerplate** | `frontend/frontend-README.md` and `cms/cms-README.md` describe a folder structure and a blog schema that don't exist here. Actively misleading — rewrite or delete. |

### 🟡 Accessibility

- Modals on `/contact`, `/sign-up` and `BookCallModal` have no `role="dialog"`, no focus trap, no Escape handler, no backdrop-click close, no body scroll lock. (`NavMobile` gets the ARIA right but still lacks a focus trap and scroll lock.)
- `<button>` nested inside `<a>` — the `<Link><Button/></Link>` pattern is used site-wide. Invalid HTML and double-focusable.
- `<label htmlFor>` pointing at controls with **no `id`**: `role`, `q1`, `q2` on `/contact`; `number` on `/sign-up`. `q1`/`q2` labels are also duplicated across the recruiter and agency branches.
- Two `<h1>`s on `/employers`.
- `alert()` used for all validation and error feedback on both forms.
- Nav hover previews are unreachable by keyboard; mobile menu tiles announce the preview title instead of the destination.
- SVG maps in `WhereWeWorkSection` have no accessible name.
- `.chevron-bounce` and the inline `slideInRight` animations escape the `prefers-reduced-motion` block.

### 🟡 Performance

- Unoptimised SVGs used as tiny icons (140 KB at 32 px, etc.) and a 123 KB logo on every page — run SVGO.
- `team/joe.png` at 496 KB.
- Bio text rendered twice in the DOM per team member.
- `useCdn: false` in the dead `GetLinkedInFeed` would hit the Sanity API on every revalidation.

